<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xinzheng</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xinzheng is a city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhengzhou">Zhengzhou</a>. It was the capital of the State of Zheng from the 8th century BCE and, after the State of Han conquered Zheng in 375 BCE, of Han until 230 BCE; parts of the old city walls survive. Tradition also names it as the home of the Yellow Emperor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xinzheng.jpg" alt="Xinzheng" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Quimbero · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Xinzheng_Pagoda.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
